    "html": "<h2>Major Forensic Breakthroughs</h2>\n<p>Through systematic local Whisper ASR dialogue extraction combined with Jerry Haendiges (<code>jjonez</code>) network logs, J. David Goldin&#39;s database, and contemporary broadcast logs, we have resolved <strong>50 previously undated or corrupted radio recordings</strong>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>1. <em>Gunsmoke</em> Mysteries Resolved</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;Ambush at Medicine Lodge&quot; ➔ <em>&quot;The Gypsum Hills Feud&quot;</em> (April 16, 1955)</strong>: Circulated for decades under the spurious collector title <em>&quot;Ambush at Medicine Lodge&quot;</em>. Internal dialogue reveals Matt Dillon and Chester interceding in a blood feud between the Peavey and Cade families in the Gypsum Hills near Medicine Lodge, featuring an on-air CBS promo for the television series <em>Mr. Citizen</em> (aired spring 1955).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;Andy Gilman&quot; ➔ <em>&quot;Bringing Down Father&quot;</em> (March 11, 1956)</strong>: Circulated in AFRS collections as undated <em>&quot;Andy Gilman&quot;</em>. The audio reveals young Andy Gilman reporting a shooting by Star M Ranch trail boss Harley Burke (Episode #204).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;Bannocks Circus&quot; ➔ <em>&quot;Wagon Show&quot;</em> (May 24, 1959)</strong>: Circulated in AFRS as <em>&quot;Bannocks Circus&quot;</em>. Dialogue reveals Chester and Doc watching an elephant on Front Street handled by Jim Conger of Bannock&#39;s Grand National Circus (Episode #371).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>2. <em>The Whistler</em> April 1948 Rebroadcast Run</h3>\n<p>Four generic recordings labeled <em>&quot;The Part 10&quot;</em> through <em>&quot;The Part 13&quot;</em> were identified as consecutive weekly Wednesday broadcasts from April 1948 on CBS West Coast:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;The Part 10&quot;</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;Bird of Prey&quot;</strong> (March 31, 1948, Ep #304)</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;The Part 11&quot;</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;What Makes a Murderer?&quot;</strong> (April 7, 1948, Ep #305, starring Frank Lovejoy and Joan Banks)</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;The Part 12&quot;</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;Till Death Do Us Part&quot;</strong> (April 14, 1948, Ep #306, starring Doris Singleton &amp; Gerald Mohr, preceded by a White House presidential address)</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;The Part 13&quot;</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;The Silent City&quot;</strong> (April 21, 1948, Ep #307)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>3. <em>Sherlock Holmes</em> Tri-Decade &quot;Blue Carbuncle&quot; Set</h3>\n<p>Three undated recordings of <em>&quot;The Adventure of the Blue Carbuncle&quot;</em> were anchored to their specific historical productions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>1948-12-26</strong>: Mutual broadcast starring John Stanley and Alfred Shirley, sponsored by Clipper Craft Clothes.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>1954-12-14</strong>: BBC Light Programme production starring Sir John Gielgud and Sir Ralph Richardson.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>1977-07-25</strong>: <em>CBS Radio Mystery Theater</em> production starring Kevin McCarthy, hosted by E.G. Marshall.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>4. <em>Fibber McGee and Molly</em> Special Recoveries</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;Xx Xx&quot; (Untitled)</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;Christmas Seal Show: Fibber McGee and Molly&quot;</strong> (1951-12-01): National Tuberculosis Association special hosted by Harlow Wilcox.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;24 On The Night Before Christmas&quot;</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;The Night Before Christmas&quot;</strong> (1946-12-24): Original Christmas Eve 1946 NBC broadcast sponsored by Johnson&#39;s Wax.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>&quot;Bob Hope&quot;</strong> ➔ <strong>&quot;June Is Dairy Month: Salute with Fibber McGee and Bob Hope&quot;</strong> (1953-06-01): California Dairy Industry Advisory Board special written by Phil Leslie.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "markdown": "# Unlocking 50 \"Date Unknown\" Radio Classics: Forensic Transcripts Solve Longstanding OTR Mysteries\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Gunsmoke, The Whistler, Sherlock Holmes, Fibber McGee, Escape, Archival Discovery\n\n---\n\n## Major Forensic Breakthroughs\n\nThrough systematic local Whisper ASR dialogue extraction combined with Jerry Haendiges (`jjonez`) network logs, J. David Goldin's database, and contemporary broadcast logs, we have resolved **50 previously undated or corrupted radio recordings**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. *Gunsmoke* Mysteries Resolved\n\n- **\"Ambush at Medicine Lodge\" ➔ *\"The Gypsum Hills Feud\"* (April 16, 1955)**: Circulated for decades under the spurious collector title *\"Ambush at Medicine Lodge\"*. Internal dialogue reveals Matt Dillon and Chester interceding in a blood feud between the Peavey and Cade families in the Gypsum Hills near Medicine Lodge, featuring an on-air CBS promo for the television series *Mr. Citizen* (aired spring 1955).\n\n- **\"Andy Gilman\" ➔ *\"Bringing Down Father\"* (March 11, 1956)**: Circulated in AFRS collections as undated *\"Andy Gilman\"*. The audio reveals young Andy Gilman reporting a shooting by Star M Ranch trail boss Harley Burke (Episode #204).\n\n- **\"Bannocks Circus\" ➔ *\"Wagon Show\"* (May 24, 1959)**: Circulated in AFRS as *\"Bannocks Circus\"*. Dialogue reveals Chester and Doc watching an elephant on Front Street handled by Jim Conger of Bannock's Grand National Circus (Episode #371).\n\n---\n\n### 2. *The Whistler* April 1948 Rebroadcast Run\n\nFour generic recordings labeled *\"The Part 10\"* through *\"The Part 13\"* were identified as consecutive weekly Wednesday broadcasts from April 1948 on CBS West Coast:\n\n- **\"The Part 10\"** ➔ **\"Bird of Prey\"** (March 31, 1948, Ep #304)\n\n- **\"The Part 11\"** ➔ **\"What Makes a Murderer?\"** (April 7, 1948, Ep #305, starring Frank Lovejoy and Joan Banks)\n\n- **\"The Part 12\"** ➔ **\"Till Death Do Us Part\"** (April 14, 1948, Ep #306, starring Doris Singleton & Gerald Mohr, preceded by a White House presidential address)\n\n- **\"The Part 13\"** ➔ **\"The Silent City\"** (April 21, 1948, Ep #307)\n\n---\n\n### 3. *Sherlock Holmes* Tri-Decade \"Blue Carbuncle\" Set\n\nThree undated recordings of *\"The Adventure of the Blue Carbuncle\"* were anchored to their specific historical productions:\n\n- **1948-12-26**: Mutual broadcast starring John Stanley and Alfred Shirley, sponsored by Clipper Craft Clothes.\n\n- **1954-12-14**: BBC Light Programme production starring Sir John Gielgud and Sir Ralph Richardson.\n\n- **1977-07-25**: *CBS Radio Mystery Theater* production starring Kevin McCarthy, hosted by E.G. Marshall.\n\n---\n\n### 4. *Fibber McGee and Molly* Special Recoveries\n\n- **\"Xx Xx\" (Untitled)** ➔ **\"Christmas Seal Show: Fibber McGee and Molly\"** (1951-12-01): National Tuberculosis Association special hosted by Harlow Wilcox.\n\n- **\"24 On The Night Before Christmas\"** ➔ **\"The Night Before Christmas\"** (1946-12-24): Original Christmas Eve 1946 NBC broadcast sponsored by Johnson's Wax.\n\n- **\"Bob Hope\"** ➔ **\"June Is Dairy Month: Salute with Fibber McGee and Bob Hope\"** (1953-06-01): California Dairy Industry Advisory Board special written by Phil Leslie.\n"
