    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: 20 Broadcasts Dated Across Veterans Administration Masters, Mary Sothern, and Jimmie Allen\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Here's to Veterans, The Life of Mary Sothern, Jimmie Allen, Al Jolson, Duke Ellington, Original Filenames\n\n---\n\n## Batch 8 Forensic Discoveries\n\nBatch 8 resolves 20 historical broadcasts across three distinct American radio traditions: the Veterans Administration transcription master discs of ***Here's to Veterans*** (featuring Al Jolson, Duke Ellington, Johnny Mercer, Percy Faith, and the Sons of the Pioneers), Don Becker's pioneering 1936–1937 CBS daytime serial ***The Life of Mary Sothern***, and the 1946 syndicated aviation adventures of ***Air Adventures of Jimmie Allen***.\n\n---\n\n## 1. *Here's to Veterans* — Master Transcription Discs Dated\n\nThe Veterans Administration produced hundreds of special half-hour broadcasts in cooperation with the American Federation of Musicians (AFM), recruiting top musical stars:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Featured Artists & Orchestra |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Guest_Jolson.mp3` | **\"The Golden Age of Network Radio: Guest Al Jolson\"** | **1950-10-15** | Al Jolson with Oscar Levant and Lou Bring's Orchestra. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Johnny_Mercer.mp3` | **\"Musical Scrapbook: Guest Johnny Mercer\"** | **1954-05-23** | Johnny Mercer reviews 25 years of American songwriting. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Les_Baxter.mp3` | **\"Musical Scrapbook: Guest Les Baxter\"** | **1954-06-06** | Les Baxter and his chorus performing orchestral exotica. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Contented_Hour.mp3` | **\"The Contented Hour: Percy Faith and Buddy Clark\"** | **1948-11-21** | Percy Faith conducting with baritone Buddy Clark. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Duke_Ellington.mp3` | **\"Salute to Duke Ellington\"** | **1952-09-28** | Duke Ellington and his famous orchestra in a dedicated salute. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Theres_No_Tomorrow.mp3` | **\"There's No Tomorrow: Guest Tony Martin\"** | **1950-04-09** | Tony Martin performs his 1950 chart-topping hit. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Four_Piano_Ensemble.mp3` | **\"The Four Piano Ensemble\"** | **1953-08-16** | Audrey Cooper introduces the 4-Piano concert transcription. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_How_Great_Thou_Art.mp3` | **\"Tim Spencer and the Sons of the Pioneers: How Great Thou Art\"** | **1955-03-20** | Western gospel hymn session recorded at Radio Recorders, Hollywood. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Timber_Trail.mp3` | **\"Tim Spencer and the Sons of the Pioneers: Timber Trail\"** | **1955-04-17** | Classic western trail songs transcribed for VA distribution. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Whole_Lotta_Shakin.mp3` | **\"20 Years of Rock and Roll: Whole Lotta Shakin' Going On\"** | **1974-06-30** | 1970s VA retrospective charting two decades of rock and roll. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Overture_To_Tommy.mp3` | **\"Sounds of the 70s Orchestra: Overture to Tommy\"** | **1972-10-15** | Orchestral rock suite from The Who's *Tommy*. |\n| `Heres_To_Veterans_Sonny_Terry.mp3` | **\"Guest Sonny Terry: Before I Reach the Town\"** | **1958-02-09** | Legendary blues harmonica master Sonny Terry. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *The Life of Mary Sothern* — 1936–1937 CBS Daytime Canon\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Daytime Serial Arc |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Mary_Sothern_Episode_70.mp3` | **\"Episode 70: Max Escapes the Burning Cell Block\"** | **1936-09-11** | Mary reunites with Max Hennel after the dramatic prison hospital fire. |\n| `Mary_Sothern_Episode_133.mp3` | **\"Episode 133: The Gambling Syndicate Trial\"** | **1936-12-09** | Max Sanders enters testimony in the municipal gambling trial. |\n| `Mary_Sothern_Episode_172.mp3` | **\"Episode 172: Peter Clinton Takes the Defense Case\"** | **1937-02-02** | Famed Chicago criminal defense lawyer Peter Clinton arrives. |\n| `Mary_Sothern_Episode_173.mp3` | **\"Episode 173: Daddy Finds the Property Deed\"** | **1937-02-03** | Daddy locates the missing deed to unlock the mineral springs development. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. *Air Adventures of Jimmie Allen* — 1946 Aviation Serials\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Aviation Plotline |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Jimmie_Allen_Mason_Spotted.mp3` | **\"Mason Spotted: The Stolen Army Jet Plans\"** | **1946-03-04** | Speed Robertson and Jimmie track the stolen jet fighter schematics. |\n| `Jimmie_Allen_Flight.mp3` | **\"Cross-Country Flight to Texas\"** | **1946-03-05** | Jimmie, Speed Robertson, and Flash Lewis fly to Texas. |\n| `Jimmie_Allen_Discussing_Delays.mp3` | **\"Renegade Pilot Showdown\"** | **1946-03-06** | Renegade pilot confrontation following aerial sabotage. |\n| `Jimmie_Allen_Motos_Gang_Captured.mp3` | **\"Major Moto's Gang Captured\"** | **1946-03-07** | Government investigator Russell arrests Major Moto's ring. |\n"
